    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.x\n\n### Description\n\nCJK punctuations are not considered as punctuations. Here's my configure:\n\n```lua\n{\n    \"echasnovski/mini.surround\",\n    opts = {\n      custom_surroundings = {\n        [\"（\"] = { output = { left = \"（\", right = \"）\" } },\n        [\"）\"] = { output = { left = \"（\", right = \"）\" } },\n        [\"【\"] = { output = { left = \"【\", right = \"】\" } },\n        [\"】\"] = { output = { left = \"【\", right = \"】\" } },\n        [\"《\"] = { output = { left = \"《\", right = \"》\" } },\n        [\"》\"] = { output = { left = \"《\", right = \"》\" } },\n        [\"‘\"] = { output = { left = \"「\", right = \"」\" } },\n        [\"’\"] = { output = { left = \"「\", right = \"」\" } },\n        [\"“\"] = { output = { left = \"『\", right = \"』\" } },\n        [\"”\"] = { output = { left = \"『\", right = \"』\" } },\n        [\"「\"] = { output = { left = \"「\", right = \"」\" } },\n        [\"」\"] = { output = { left = \"「\", right = \"」\" } },\n        [\"『\"] = { output = { left = \"『\", right = \"』\" } },\n        [\"』\"] = { output = { left = \"『\", right = \"』\" } },\n      },\n    },\n  }\n```\n\nHowever it throws an error \"Input must be single character: alphanumeric, punctuation, or space.\"\n\nThis can work in [vim-surround](https://github.com/tpope/vim-surround).\n\nThen I've found where the error occurs:\n\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.surround/blob/aa5e245829dd12d8ff0c96ef11da28681d6049aa/lua/mini/surround.lua#L1951-L1961\n\nCJK punctuations are not matched by Lua's pattern.\n\nHere's [a general regex that can match these punctuations](https://regex101.com/r/hSJdIY/2): `[\\u2000-\\u206F\\u3000-\\u303F\\uFF00-\\uFFEF]`:\n- `\\u2000-\\u206F` stands for [General Punctuation](https://www.unicode.org/charts/PDF/U2000.pdf), including pairs like `“”`\n- `\\u3000-\\u303F` stands for [CJK Symbols and Punctuation](https://unicode.org/charts/PDF/U3000.pdf), including pairs like `「」`\n- `\\uFF00-\\uFFEF` stands for [Halfwidth and Fullwidth Forms](https://www.unicode.org/charts/PDF/UFF00.pdf), including fullwidth-form punctuations like `，`(no pairs)\n\nMaybe I miss something, but this can cover most.\n\nHowever Lua's pattern matching seems to be a bit difficult for me since it works byte by byte. So I come here for help. Thanks in advance.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n`opts` is shown above, you can have a check easily.",
