            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nI am not entirely sure about the reasoning for adding this limitation on surrounding ids to begin with. As it is present right from the beginning of 'mini.surround' (and 'mini.nvim', for what it's worth) it might as well be that I thought that there are some issues with having multibyte characters as surrounding ids. I'll take a closer look.\n\nAs I don't have a setup to enter CJK character, would you mind doing some experiment for me, please? Could you:\n- Execute the following code: `:lua char = vim.fn.getcharstr()`\n- Press one of the characters with which you get the \"Input must be single character: alphanumeric, punctuation, or space.\" message.\n- Execute the following code: `:lua print(vim.inspect(char))` . Does it show the character you pressed in full (i.e. the way you'd expect to use it in `custom_surroundings`) surrounded by quotes?",
